1. d4 { [%clk 0:04:56] } 1... g5? { Black just... blunders the first move. } { [%csl Rg5][%cal Rc1g5] [%clk 0:04:58] } 2. Bxg5 { [%clk 0:04:51] } 2... f6 { [%clk 0:04:58] } 3. e4 { [%clk 0:04:39] } 3... h5 { "Jeez relax." - Daniel Naroditsky Nov, 2020 } { [%csl Rh5][%cal Rd1h5] [%clk 0:04:58] } (3... fxg5 { Black, in fact, cannot take the bishop as it blunders... } 4. Qh5# { ... checkmate! }) 4. Be2 { Building the battery to attack the pawn. } { [%csl Rh5][%cal Rd1h5] [%clk 0:04:23] } 4... e5 { [%clk 0:04:41] } 5. Bxh5+ { [%clk 0:04:17] } 5... Ke7 { [%clk 0:04:38] } 6. Be3 { Defending the pawn and preventing the queen from being overloaded as the only defender of the light squared bishop. } { [%csl Gd4,Gh5][%cal Ge3d4,Gd1d4,Gd1h5,Rh8h5] [%clk 0:03:56] } 6... d6 { [%clk 0:04:17] } 7. Nc3 { [%csl Gd5][%cal Gc3d5] [%clk 0:03:39] } 7... c6 { [%clk 0:04:10] } 8. Be2 { Enabling Ng3. } { [%csl Gf3][%cal Gg1f3] [%clk 0:03:17] } 8... Bh6 { [%clk 0:03:53] } 9. Bxh6 { [%clk 0:03:14] } 9... Nxh6 { [%clk 0:03:49] } 10. Nf3 { [%clk 0:03:13] } 10... Ng4 { White side should white look to castle on? } { [%clk 0:03:38] } 11. Qd2 { Looking to castle long as the kingside files are half open. } { [%csl Ga1,Rh2][%cal Ga1d1,Ge1c1,Rh8h2] [%clk 0:03:02] } 11... Na6 { White can't castle quite yet. } { [%csl Rf2][%cal Rg4f2] [%clk 0:03:17] } 12. h3 { White isn't attacking the knight yet because taking the knight would hang the h1 rook. } { [%csl Rh1][%cal Rh8h1] [%clk 0:02:59] } 12... Nh6 { Black chooses to get out of the way immediately. } { [%clk 0:03:13] } 13. O-O-O { White can now castle. } { [%clk 0:02:55] } 13... Nb4 { [%clk 0:02:57] } (13... Nc7 14. Rhg1 { Another idea for white. Preparing g4-g5 to crack open the center. } { [%csl Gg5][%cal Gg2g4,Gg4g5] }) 14. a3 { [%clk 0:02:54] } 14... Na6 { Should white open the center? } { [%clk 0:02:50] } 15. dxe5 { Yes! With the development advantage and black's king stuck in the center, white would like to rip open the center to setup an attack. } { [%clk 0:02:33] } 15... fxe5 { Black weakens the g5 square. Are there any tactics that this enables? } { [%csl Bg5] [%clk 0:02:46] } 16. Nxe5 { Yes! Black's queen is x-rayed and white can take advantage by "sacrificing" the knight. } { [%csl Rd8,Rd2,Rd1,Gg5][%cal Rd1d8,Gd2g5] [%clk 0:01:57] } 16... dxe5 { [%clk 0:02:44] } 17. Qg5+ { [%clk 0:01:55] } 17... Ke8 { No need to take the queen just yet, white has a mate. } { [%clk 0:02:20] } 18. Bh5+ { [%clk 0:01:36] } 18... Nf7 { [%clk 0:02:16] } 19. Rxd8# { 1-0 White wins by checkmate. } { [%clk 0:01:35] } 1-0


