{ THEMES and Things to Look For
- When considering a discovery, ensure that the opponent cannot simultaneously take the piece which moved to allow the discovery and defend the discovered attack.

Games referenced

Stream footage here: https://youtu.be/hzotV0aslmY?t=1955
Game played here: https://www.chess.com/live/game/5678526234 }
1. d4 { [%clk 0:04:56] } 1... d5 { [%clk 0:04:55] } 2. a3 { Passive move from white } { [%clk 0:04:55] } 2... Nf6 { Black develops normally. } { [%clk 0:04:50] } 3. Nf3 { [%clk 0:04:54] } 3... Bf5 { Developing the bishop before locking in the pawn chain. } { [%csl Ge6][%cal Ge7e6] [%clk 0:04:36] } (3... e6 { Suboptimal due to blocking the bishop in. This does occurs in the queens gambit, but it is okay there. } { [%csl Ge6][%cal Gc8e6] }) (3... Bg4 { No reason to allow this line. } 4. Ne5 Bf5) 4. Nc3 { [%clk 0:04:53] } 4... e6 { [%clk 0:04:34] } 5. Ne5 { [%clk 0:04:51] } 5... Bd6 { White moves the same piece twice in the opening giving black tempo to continue developing. } { [%clk 0:04:27] } 6. Nxf7?? { White sacrifices the knight with no compensation. There is no follow up to this attack. } { [%clk 0:04:50] } (6. e3 { What is black's plan here? } 6... O-O 7. Be2 c5 { Undermining the defender of the knight. Note that white is unable to play c3 due to the knight in the way. } { [%csl Rd4][%cal Rc5d4,Gd4e5] }) 6... Kxf7 { [%clk 0:04:25] } 7. Bg5 { [%clk 0:04:45] } 7... h6 { Trying to pick the bishop away. } { [%clk 0:04:04] } 8. Bxf6 { [%clk 0:04:43] } 8... Qxf6 { [%clk 0:04:00] } 9. e3 { [%clk 0:04:40] } 9... Rf8 { Ideas of "castling by hand". } { [%csl Gg8][%cal Gf7g8] [%clk 0:03:57] } 10. Nb5 { [%clk 0:04:39] } 10... Kg8 { [%clk 0:03:53] } 11. Nxd6 { [%clk 0:04:34] } 11... cxd6 { [%clk 0:03:52] } 12. Bb5 { Black has built up a nice battery here, but the discovered checkmate attack can be easily stopped. } { [%csl Rf2][%cal Rf8f2] [%clk 0:04:28] } 12... Qg6 { Instead, black goes for the g2 pawn. } { [%clk 0:02:54] } (12... Bxc2?? { This is a blunder as... } 13. Qxc2 { ... white is able to take the bishop and simultaneously defend the f2 pawn. } { [%csl Rf2][%cal Gc2f2,Rf8f2] }) 13. O-O { [%clk 0:04:21] } 13... Bh3 { White's pawn is pinned by the so white must give up the rook to stop checkmate. } { [%csl Rf1,Rg1][%cal Rh3f1,Rg6g1] [%clk 0:02:43] } 14. Qf3?? { Oops. Maybe white will give up the queen instead. } { [%clk 0:04:11] } 14... Rxf3 { [%clk 0:02:42] } 15. Bd7 { [%clk 0:04:03] } 15... Qxg2# { 0-1 Black wins by checkmate. } { [%clk 0:02:40] } 0-1


