{ THEMES and Things to Look For
- Pawn structure isn't everything, especially when there is compensation (in this game winning material).
- Note where pieces can or can't retreat to in the opening, this can be a clue that there might be a trapped piece or a way to win material.

Stream footage here: https://youtu.be/OwrIaWwPJvM?t=697
Game played here: https://www.chess.com/live/game/5802980332 }
1. e4 { [%c_effect e4;square;e4;type;Book] [%clk 0:05:00] } 1... c5 { [%clk 0:04:59] } 2. Bc4 { Sicilian! } { [%clk 0:04:59] } 2... Nc6 { [%clk 0:04:58] } 3. b3? { White wasting a tempo to prepare fianchettoing the bishop. } { [%clk 0:04:59] } 3... Nf6 { [%clk 0:04:48] } 4. d3? { This combined with fianchettoing the dark squared bishop is a mistake because the light squared bishop no longer has a way to retreat.
Now white has to play something like d4 or b4 to save the bishop which will give up a pawn. } { [%cal Gd3d4,Gb3b4] [%clk 0:04:55] } (4. Bb2) 4... e6 { [%clk 0:04:45] } 5. Bb2? { [%clk 0:04:52] } 5... d5 { Now black has a way to win a minor piece. } { [%clk 0:04:44] } 6. exd5 { [%clk 0:04:49] } 6... exd5 { Bishop seems like it gets away, but... } { [%csl Gb5][%cal Gc4b5] [%clk 0:04:43] } 7. Bb5 { [%clk 0:04:48] } 7... Qa5+ { [%clk 0:04:28] } 8. Nc3 { [%clk 0:04:44] } 8... d4 { [%clk 0:04:21] } 9. Bxc6+ { [%clk 0:04:42] } 9... bxc6 { [%clk 0:04:20] } 10. Qe2+ { [%clk 0:04:37] } 10... Be7 { [%clk 0:04:15] } 11. Nf3 { [%clk 0:04:34] } 11... dxc3 { ... white loses a minor piece in the exchange due to the bishop effectively being trapped.
This looks like an ugly pawn structure for black, but black has more than enough compensation being up a full minor piece. } { [%csl Bc3,Bc5,Bc6] [%clk 0:04:14] } 12. Bc1 { Can black castle here even though the bishop would be left hanging? } { [%csl Re7][%cal Re2e7] [%clk 0:04:31] } 12... O-O { Yes, because the bishop is protected by pinning tactics. } { [%clk 0:03:59] } 13. O-O { [%clk 0:04:26] } (13. Qxe7 Re8 { [%csl Re1,Re7][%cal Re8e1] } 14. Qxe8+ Nxe8 { Forcing the loss of the queen. }) 13... Qc7 { Now needing to defend the bishop because there is no longer a pin available on the e file. } { [%csl Ge7][%cal Gc7e7] [%clk 0:03:54] } 14. Bg5 { [%clk 0:04:23] } 14... Bg4 { [%clk 0:03:52] } 15. Qe3 { [%clk 0:04:11] } 15... Nd5 { [%csl Re3,Ge7][%cal Rd5e3,Gd5e7] [%clk 0:03:42] } 16. Qe4 { [%clk 0:03:34] } 16... Bxf3 { Removing the defender from the bishop. } { [%csl Rg5,Re4][%cal Re7g5,Rf3e4] [%clk 0:03:41] } 17. Qxf3 { [%clk 0:03:29] } 17... Bxg5 { [%clk 0:03:40] } 0-1


