[ChapterName "Game 120: Philidor Defense, Exchange Variation (White, ELO 1798)"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/dSNQO9Uq/K7nRwjY8"]
[Annotator "https://lichess.org/@/rudisco"]

{ THEMES and Things to Look For
- Losing castling rights is not as much of a problem when queens are off the board.
- Pawn structure isn't everything, sometimes we will avoid moves that seem to "ruin" the opponent's structure because, while aesthetically ugly, will actually strengthen their position.

Stream footage here: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n781_V5I0ac
Game played here: https://www.chess.com/live/game/5914662573 }
1. e4 d6 2. d4 Nf6 3. Nc3 e5 { Philidor stars here } 4. Nf3 { Main line, developing the knight. } (4. dxe5 { Intending to trade queens. } { [%csl Rd8][%cal Rd1d8] } 4... dxe5 5. Qxd8+ Kxd8 { The position here remains pretty equal. Once queens are off the board, not being able to castle is less of a problem. }) 4... exd4 5. Nxd4 Be7 6. Bd3 { Reinforcing the central pawn while developing the bishop. } { [%csl Ge4][%cal Gd3e4] } 6... Nc6 7. Nb3 (7. Nxc6 bxc6 { Either line is okay, but Danya prefers the line as played since this allows black to prepare d5. } { [%csl Gd5][%cal Gd6d5] } 8. Bg5 Rb8 { Black also has ideas of controlling the half open b-file. } { [%csl Rb2][%cal Rb8b2] }) 7... O-O 8. O-O Be6 (8... d5?? { Falling into a nasty discovered check. } 9. exd5 Qxd5 10. Bxh7+ Kxh7 11. Qxd5) 9. f4 { This may seem like a passive move, why not develop the dark squared bishop? } 9... Re8 { We could play f5, but the pawn is preventing black's knight from outposting. } { [%csl Re5][%cal Rf4e5,Gc6e5] } 10. Qf3 d5 (10... Bf8 { Black's better move. Looks passive, but black opens up the file for their rook. } { [%cal Re8e6] }) 11. e5 { Keeping the position closed } 11... Ne4? { Black blundering the exchange, losing a pawn for no compensation. } 12. Nxe4 dxe4 13. Qxe4 { [%csl Rh7][%cal Re4h7] } 13... g6 14. f5 Bxf5 (14... Bd5 15. Qf4 Nxe5 { Winning a pawn, because... } 16. Qxe5 Bc5+ 17. Nxc5 Rxe5 { ... a discovered attack, this time for black. }) 15. Rxf5 { Sacrificing the rook to gain mating threats. } { [%csl Rh7][%cal Re4h7] } 15... gxf5 16. Qxf5 1-0


