{ THEMES and Things to Look For
- Try to look for moves that cement your opponent's weaknesses. In this game, white exploits black's dark squared weakness after black plays c6 and e6

Stream footage here: https://youtu.be/n781_V5I0ac?t=592
Game played here: https://www.chess.com/live/game/5914695254 }
1. e4 { [%clk 0:05:00] } 1... g6 { [%clk 0:04:59] } 2. d4 { [%clk 0:04:59] } 2... Bg7 { [%clk 0:04:57] } 3. Nc3 { [%clk 0:04:56] } 3... c6 { Black plays a modern Caro-Kann hybrid and preparing d5. } { [%csl Gd5][%cal Gd7d5] [%clk 0:04:55] } 4. Bc4 { Stopping d5. } { [%csl Rd5][%cal Rc4d5,Gd7d5] [%clk 0:04:40] } 4... e6 { Black continuing to prepare d5, but leaves d6 and f6 very weak. } { [%csl Bd6,Bf6] [%clk 0:04:51] } 5. e5 { Cementing black's weaknesses. } { [%csl Rd6,Rf6][%cal Re5d6,Re5f6] [%clk 0:04:17] } 5... d5 { [%clk 0:04:50] } 6. exd6 { [%clk 0:04:15] } 6... Qxd6 { Black's light squared bishop is blocked. } { [%cal Gc8e6] [%clk 0:04:48] } 7. Nf3 { [%clk 0:04:10] } 7... Nf6 { [%clk 0:04:44] } 8. O-O { [%clk 0:04:07] } 8... Nd5 { [%clk 0:04:40] } 9. Ne4 { [%clk 0:03:59] } 9... Qd8 { [%clk 0:04:36] } 10. Bg5 { [%clk 0:03:46] } 10... Nf6? { Black pinning their knight. } { [%csl Rd8][%cal Rg5d8] [%clk 0:04:23] } (10... f6 11. Bh4 { Playing f6 here would have been better, but black's kingside becomes very weak. White has ideas of assaulting the e pawn on the half open file and if black castles there is a lot of "space" for white to attack through. } { [%csl Bh7,Bg6,Bf6,Be6,Ge1][%cal Gf1e1,Re1e6] }) 11. Ne5 { [%clk 0:03:28] } 11... O-O { White would like to put more pressure on this knight. } { [%csl Bf6] [%clk 0:04:16] } 12. Qf3 { Black will lose the exchange. } { [%csl Rf6][%cal Rf3f6,Re4f6,Rg5f6] [%clk 0:03:11] } 12... Qxd4 { [%clk 0:04:10] } 13. Nxf6+ { [%clk 0:03:08] } 13... Bxf6 { [%clk 0:04:08] } 14. Bxf6 { It's no surprise that the exchange happens on black's weak f6 square. } { [%csl Bf6] [%clk 0:03:08] } 14... Qxc4 { [%clk 0:04:05] } 15. Nxc4 { 1-0 White wins. } { [%clk 0:03:06] } 1-0


