{ THEMES and Things to Look For
- Another hypermodern opening, black aims to control the center from a distance.

Stream footage here: https://youtu.be/7uxRcomJo7I?t=1183
Game played here: https://www.chess.com/live/game/5930953026 }
1. e4 { [%clk 0:05:00] } 1... g6 { Starting with the Modern Defense.
The first time the Modern was played was in 1842. Only played a handful (literally) times before 1950. } { [%clk 0:04:56] } 2. d4 { [%clk 0:04:58] } 2... Bg7 { [%clk 0:04:55] } 3. Nc3 { [%clk 0:04:39] } 3... d6 { [%clk 0:04:52] } 4. f4 { Starting the Austrian attack, first played in 1951 in Switzerland. The origins of "Austrian" remain a mystery. } { [%clk 0:04:36] } 4... Nf6 { [%clk 0:04:43] } 5. Nf3 { [%clk 0:04:34] } 5... O-O { [%clk 0:04:39] } 6. e5 { [%clk 0:04:29] } 6... dxe5 { [%clk 0:04:37] } 7. fxe5 { Where to put the knight? } { [%clk 0:04:28] } 7... Nd5 { [%clk 0:04:11] } (7... Ne8 { Not great, inactive space for the knight. }) (7... Nh5 { Knight on the rim is grim. }) (7... Ng4 8. h3 Nh6 { White easily pushes the knight to the rim. }) 8. Bc4 { Should black trade? } { [%csl Rc3][%cal Rd5c3] [%clk 0:04:23] } 8... Be6 { [%clk 0:03:41] } (8... Nxc3 9. bxc3 { Trading allows white to strengthen their center pawn chain. } { [%csl Gd4,Gb1,Rb7][%cal Gc3d4,Ga1b1,Rb1b7] }) 9. Ng5 { White's bishop is undefended. } { [%csl Rc4][%cal Re6c4] [%clk 0:04:05] } (9. Bb3 { Better move for white to secure the bishop. }) 9... Nxc3 { Discovered attack! } { [%csl Rc4][%cal Re6c4] [%clk 0:03:20] } 10. Nxe6 { White tries to get out of this by attacking the queen. } { [%csl Rd1,Rd8][%cal Rc3d1,Re6d8] [%clk 0:04:03] } 10... Nxd1 { [%clk 0:03:10] } 11. Nxd8 { [%clk 0:04:01] } 11... Rxd8 { Attacking the hanging pawn. } { [%csl Rd4][%cal Rd8d4] [%clk 0:03:09] } 12. O-O { [%clk 0:03:52] } (12. Kxd1 { If white takes immediately... } 12... Rxd4+ { ... then black wins a second pawn. }) 12... Rxd4 { [%clk 0:02:33] } 13. Bxf7+ { [%clk 0:03:46] } 13... Kh8 { [%clk 0:02:31] } 14. c3 { [%clk 0:03:39] } 14... Rd8 { [%clk 0:02:23] } 15. Bg5 { [%clk 0:03:30] } (15. Bb3 { White should have fully trapped the knight here. } 15... Nxc3 (15... Nxb2 16. Bxb2 { This is not as good because it allows white to develop the dark squared bishop. }) 16. bxc3 Bxe5 { Best way for black to give back the knight. }) 15... Nxb2 { [%clk 0:02:09] } 16. Bxe7 { [%clk 0:03:28] } 16... Rc8 { This looks scary for black, but the king is protected (for now) and black is up a piece. } { [%clk 0:02:08] } 17. Rab1 { [%clk 0:03:08] } 17... Nc6 { Developing and attacking the hanging bishop. } { [%csl Re7][%cal Rc6e7] [%clk 0:01:53] } 18. Bf6 { [%clk 0:03:03] } 18... Nd3 { Now we get the knight out of danger. } { [%clk 0:01:44] } 19. Rxb7 { [%clk 0:02:57] } 19... Ndxe5 { [%clk 0:01:39] } 20. Bxg7+ { [%clk 0:02:55] } 20... Kxg7 { [%clk 0:01:38] } 21. Bd5 { [%clk 0:02:54] } 21... Rab8 { [%clk 0:01:25] } 22. Rxb8 { [%clk 0:02:45] } 22... Rxb8 { [%clk 0:01:17] } 23. Re1 { [%clk 0:02:42] } 23... Rb2 { <br /><br />Game may have continued... } { [%clk 0:01:08] } (23... h3 24. Rc2 Bxc6 25. Nxc6 Rb1 26. Ne7 Rb7 { -4.94 }) 0-1


