{ THEMES and Things to Look For
- Flexibility. If your opponent does something unconventional, don't feel committed to following the initial opening ideas. In this game, black plays a hypermodern opening, but white does not seize the center.
- When your opponent attacks on the flanks, a good response is to attack in the center!

Stream footage here: https://youtu.be/SXsVWpN8e1A?t=2044
Game played here: https://www.chess.com/live/game/6009890435 }
1. e4 { [%clk 0:05:00] } 1... Nf6 { [%clk 0:04:59] } 2. e5 { [%clk 0:04:58] } 2... Nd5 { [%clk 0:04:58] } 3. Nc3 { [%clk 0:04:57] } 3... Nb6 { [%clk 0:04:46] } (3... Nxc3 4. dxc3 { This helps white accelerate their development. } { [%cal Gc1f4] }) 4. a4 { [%clk 0:04:50] } 4... a5 { [%clk 0:04:44] } 5. Bb5 { [%clk 0:04:37] } (5. d4 { This is the mainline. }) 5... c6 { [%clk 0:04:18] } 6. Bd3? { Obstructs the pawn. } { [%csl Gd4][%cal Gd2d4] [%clk 0:04:36] } 6... d5 { Since white did not seize the center, black and start laying a claim. } { [%clk 0:04:17] } 7. Nce2 { [%clk 0:04:20] } (7. exd6 { Probably a better move for white. } 7... exd6) 7... g6 { [%csl Gg7,Re5][%cal Gf8g7,Rg7e5] [%clk 0:04:03] } 8. b3 { [%clk 0:04:12] } 8... Bg7 { [%clk 0:04:03] } 9. Bb2 { [%clk 0:04:11] } 9... O-O { [%clk 0:04:02] } 10. h4 { [%clk 0:04:09] } 10... c5 { Preparing Nc6. } { [%csl Gc6][%cal Gb8c6] [%clk 0:03:49] } 11. Nf4 { [%clk 0:03:51] } 11... Nc6 { [%clk 0:03:36] } 12. Nf3 { [%clk 0:03:30] } 12... Bg4 { Pinning the knight with ideas of winning the e5 pawn. } { [%csl Rd1,Re5][%cal Rg4d1,Rg7e5,Rc6e5] [%clk 0:03:34] } 13. Qe2 { [%clk 0:03:29] } 13... Qc7 { Applying more pressure onto the pawn. } { [%csl Re5][%cal Rc7e5,Rc6e5,Rg7e5] [%clk 0:03:15] } 14. O-O-O { [%clk 0:03:06] } 14... Bxf3 { [%clk 0:03:08] } 15. Qxf3 { How should black take the pawn? } { [%clk 0:03:04] } 15... Nxe5 { Taking white's pawn with tempo. } { [%csl Rf3][%cal Re5f3] [%clk 0:02:56] } (15... Bxe5 16. Nxd5 { This allows white to re-take the pawn with tempo. } { [%csl Rc7][%cal Rd5c7] }) 16. Nxd5 { Nice idea from white, equalizing material. } { [%csl Rc7,Rf3][%cal Rd5c7,Re5f3] [%clk 0:02:13] } 16... Qd6 { [%clk 0:02:55] } 17. Bxe5 { [%clk 0:01:56] } 17... Qxe5 { The hanging b6 knight is protected by threatening checkmate. } { [%csl Rb2,Bb6][%cal Rg7b2] [%clk 0:02:42] } 18. Nc3 { [%clk 0:01:54] } 18... c4 { Attempting to open up the queenside to attack white's king. } { [%clk 0:02:28] } 19. Qxb7?? { [%clk 0:01:41]